/* RemoveArray_r: intermediate level of RemoveArray, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: state every count in one form, the fixed set of kept positions cut by a growing interval:
   card(S /\ (0..xx - 1)), with S = {ii | ii : 0..max_IDX & array(ii) /= value}. This is the form a
   counting loop keeps, the one the proof lines of card_ar and compte_ar close, whereas a comprehension
   whose domain depends on the position does not reach them. The proof that the two forms agree,
   {jj | jj : 0..xx - 1 & array(jj) /= value} = S /\ (0..xx - 1) for xx : 0..max_IDX, is thus done once,
   here, away from the loop.
   Nothing else changes: rr still ranges over ran(array), which the loop keeps cell by cell, and the
   couple form of the moved cell stays, so it needs no proof that the position is in the domain of rr.
   S is written with the bound name ii everywhere, as in RemoveArray, and the two quantifiers over
   positions use xx: the rule has one joker for each.
   array stays the concrete variable of RemoveArray; set_cell and the initialisation are unchanged.
   Same shape as SelectionSort_r and ReverseArray_r, the levels with an inherited concrete variable
   BART has refined: an INVARIANT clause restating the type of array, and an ANY, taken by a structure
   rule. */
REFINEMENT
    RemoveArray_r

REFINES
    RemoveArray

SEES
    Ctx_RemoveArray

INVARIANT
    array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT

INITIALISATION
    array := (0..max_IDX) * {0}

OPERATIONS

    set_cell(pos, val) =
    PRE
        pos : IDX &
        val : INT
    THEN
        array(pos) := val
    END;

    kept <-- remove(value) =
    PRE
        value : INT
    THEN
        ANY rr, nb WHERE
            rr : (0..max_IDX) --> ran(array) &
            nb : NAT &
            nb = card({ii | ii : 0..max_IDX & array(ii) /= value}) &
            !xx.(xx : 0..max_IDX & array(xx) /= value =>
                 (card({ii | ii : 0..max_IDX & array(ii) /= value} /\ (0..xx - 1)) |-> array(xx)) : rr) &
            !xx.(xx : nb..max_IDX => rr(xx) = array(xx))
        THEN
            array := rr ||
            kept := nb
        END
    END

END
